Given below are two statements :
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement 1:</strong></span></td><td>Highest oxidation state of a metal is exhibited in its oxide or fluoride only.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement 2:</strong></span></td><td>Both oxide and fluoride ions are able to oxidise metals.</td></tr></tbody></table>In light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :<br>&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="min-width: 300px;"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><strong>Statement 1</strong> is true, <strong>Statement 2</strong> is false.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td><strong>Statement 1</strong> is false, <strong>Statement 2</strong> is true.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Both <strong>Statements 1 </strong>and <strong>Statement 2 </strong>are true.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Both<strong> Statements 1</strong> and <strong>Statement 2</strong>&nbsp;are false.</td></tr></tbody></table>
